# AP Chemistry — master IDs 04-xxx plus research expansion. Pending teacher review.
@subject ap-chemistry | AP Chemistry | AP 化学 | Chem | rose | 6
@desc Atoms, bonding, reactions, kinetics, thermodynamics, equilibrium and acids/bases.
@framework Unit titles follow the AP Chemistry course framework (9 units).

@unit 1 | Atomic Structure and Properties | 原子结构与性质
- mole | 摩尔 | The amount of substance containing 6.022 × 10²³ particles (Avogadro's number) | 物质的量单位，1 mol 含 6.022×10²³ 个粒子。 | 18 g of water contains one mole of H₂O molecules. | 1 | #04-001
- molar mass | 摩尔质量 | The mass of one mole of a substance, in g/mol | 1 摩尔物质的质量，数值上等于相对分子（原子）质量。 | The molar mass of CO₂ is 44 g/mol. | 1
- isotope | 同位素 | Atoms of the same element with different numbers of neutrons | 质子数相同、中子数不同的原子。 | Carbon-12 and carbon-14 are isotopes. | 1
- electron configuration | 电子排布 | The arrangement of electrons in an atom's orbitals | 电子在原子轨道中的分布方式，如 1s²2s²2p⁶。 | The electron configuration of sodium ends in 3s¹. | 2
- photoelectron spectroscopy | 光电子能谱 | A technique measuring the energy needed to remove electrons, revealing electron shells and subshells | 测量移除电子所需能量的技术，可显示电子层和亚层结构。 | A PES spectrum with peaks in a 2:2:6 ratio indicates neon-like 1s²2s²2p⁶. | 3
- ionization energy | 电离能 | The energy required to remove an electron from a gaseous atom | 从气态原子中移除一个电子所需的能量，同周期从左到右总体增大。 | Ionization energy increases across a period because effective nuclear charge increases. | 2
- Coulomb's law | 库仑定律 | The force between charges is proportional to the product of charges and inversely proportional to the square of the distance | 电荷间作用力与电荷乘积成正比，与距离平方成反比，是解释周期规律的核心。 | Coulomb's law explains why smaller atoms hold their valence electrons more tightly. | 3
- electronegativity | 电负性 | An atom's tendency to attract shared electrons in a bond | 原子在化学键中吸引共用电子的能力，氟最强。 | Because oxygen is more electronegative than hydrogen, the O–H bond is polar. | 2 | #04-005

@unit 2 | Compound Structure and Properties | 化合物的结构与性质
- ionic bond | 离子键 | Electrostatic attraction between oppositely charged ions | 阴阳离子之间的静电吸引，通常存在于金属与非金属之间。 | NaCl is held together by ionic bonds in a crystal lattice. | 1 | #04-006
  vs: covalent bond
- covalent bond | 共价键 | A bond formed by sharing electron pairs between atoms | 原子之间通过共用电子对形成的化学键。 | Each C–H bond in methane is a covalent bond. | 1 | #04-007
  vs: ionic bond
- Lewis structure | 路易斯结构 | A diagram showing valence electrons, bonds and lone pairs in a molecule | 表示分子中价电子、化学键和孤对电子的结构式。 | The Lewis structure of CO₂ shows two double bonds. | 2
- VSEPR theory | 价层电子对互斥理论 | A model predicting molecular shape from repulsion among electron domains | 根据中心原子周围电子对的互斥预测分子几何构型。 | VSEPR predicts that water is bent because of two lone pairs. | 2
- hybridization | 杂化 | The mixing of atomic orbitals to form new hybrid orbitals | 原子轨道混合形成新的杂化轨道，如 sp³、sp²、sp。 | Carbon in methane is sp³ hybridized. | 3
- resonance | 共振 | When a molecule can be represented by two or more valid Lewis structures | 分子可以用多个合理的路易斯结构表示，真实结构是它们的平均。 | Ozone has two resonance structures. | 3

@unit 3 | Properties of Substances and Mixtures | 物质与混合物的性质
- intermolecular forces | 分子间作用力 | Attractions between separate molecules, such as London dispersion, dipole-dipole and hydrogen bonding | 分子之间的吸引力，包括色散力、偶极-偶极作用和氢键。分子间作用力越强，沸点越高。 | Water's hydrogen bonding gives it a higher boiling point than H₂S. | 2 | #04-008
  mis: Breaking intermolecular forces breaks covalent bonds — boiling separates molecules but leaves bonds intact.
  vs: covalent bond
- London dispersion forces | 伦敦色散力 | Weak temporary attractions from instantaneous dipoles, present in all molecules | 由瞬时偶极产生的弱吸引，存在于所有分子中，电子越多越强。 | I₂ is a solid at room temperature because of strong London dispersion forces. | 2
- ideal gas law | 理想气体定律 | PV = nRT, relating pressure, volume, moles and temperature of an ideal gas | 理想气体状态方程，温度必须用开尔文。 | Doubling the temperature in kelvins at constant volume doubles the pressure. | 2
- molarity | 摩尔浓度 | Moles of solute per liter of solution | 每升溶液中溶质的物质的量（mol/L）。 | Dissolving 0.5 mol NaCl in 1.0 L of solution gives 0.5 M. | 1 | #04-002
- Beer-Lambert law | 比尔-朗伯定律 | Absorbance is proportional to concentration, A = εbc | 吸光度与浓度成正比，用于分光光度法测浓度。 | Using the Beer-Lambert law, a solution with twice the absorbance has twice the concentration. | 3

@unit 4 | Chemical Reactions | 化学反应
- stoichiometry | 化学计量关系 | The quantitative relationships among reactants and products in a balanced equation | 根据配平方程式中的比例计算反应物与产物的量。 | Stoichiometry predicts that 2 mol H₂ react with 1 mol O₂. | 2 | #04-003
- limiting reactant | 限制反应物 | The reactant that is completely consumed first and limits product formation | 最先被完全消耗、决定产物最大量的反应物。 | With 2 mol H₂ and 2 mol O₂, hydrogen is the limiting reactant. | 2 | #04-004
  mis: The limiting reactant is the one with the smaller mass — compare moles using the balanced equation.
- precipitation reaction | 沉淀反应 | A reaction in which two solutions form an insoluble solid | 两种溶液混合生成难溶固体的反应。 | Mixing AgNO₃ and NaCl forms an AgCl precipitate. | 2
- net ionic equation | 净离子方程式 | An equation showing only the species that change in a reaction | 只写出实际参与反应的离子和物质，省略旁观离子。 | The net ionic equation for neutralization is H⁺ + OH⁻ → H₂O. | 2
- oxidation | 氧化 | Loss of electrons | 失去电子（氧化数升高）。口诀 OIL RIG。 | In the reaction, zinc is oxidized from 0 to +2. | 2 | #04-018
  vs: reduction
- reduction | 还原 | Gain of electrons | 得到电子（氧化数降低）。 | Cu²⁺ is reduced to copper metal. | 2 | #04-019
  vs: oxidation
- titration | 滴定 | A technique using a measured volume of a solution of known concentration to find an unknown concentration | 用已知浓度的溶液测定未知溶液浓度的方法，在等当点反应物恰好完全反应。 | At the equivalence point of the titration, moles of acid equal moles of base. | 2 | #04-020

@unit 5 | Kinetics | 化学动力学
- reaction rate | 反应速率 | The change in concentration of a reactant or product per unit time | 单位时间内反应物或产物浓度的变化。 | Increasing temperature increases the reaction rate. | 2 | #04-012
- rate law | 速率方程 | An experimentally determined equation relating rate to reactant concentrations, rate = k[A]ᵐ[B]ⁿ | 由实验确定的速率与浓度关系式，反应级数不能从方程式系数直接得出。 | Doubling [A] quadruples the rate, so the rate law is second order in A. | 3 | #04-013
  mis: Exponents in the rate law come from coefficients — they must be determined experimentally.
- activation energy | 活化能 | The minimum energy needed for a reaction to occur | 反应发生所需的最低能量，催化剂降低活化能。 | A catalyst speeds up the reaction by providing a pathway with lower activation energy. | 2
- catalyst | 催化剂 | A substance that speeds up a reaction without being consumed | 加快反应速率而本身不被消耗的物质，不改变平衡位置。 | A catalyst does not change the equilibrium constant. | 2
- reaction mechanism | 反应机理 | The sequence of elementary steps by which a reaction occurs | 反应发生的一系列基元步骤，最慢的一步决定速率。 | The slowest elementary step in a mechanism is the rate-determining step. | 3

@unit 6 | Thermodynamics | 热力学
- enthalpy | 焓 | A state function whose change equals heat transferred at constant pressure | 状态函数，恒压下其变化等于吸收或放出的热量。ΔH < 0 为放热。 | Combustion reactions have negative enthalpy changes. | 2 | #04-009
- exothermic | 放热的 | Releasing heat to the surroundings (ΔH < 0) | 向环境释放热量的过程。 | Hand warmers rely on an exothermic reaction. | 1
  vs: endothermic
- endothermic | 吸热的 | Absorbing heat from the surroundings (ΔH > 0) | 从环境吸收热量的过程。 | Cold packs work because dissolving ammonium nitrate is endothermic. | 1
  vs: exothermic
- specific heat capacity | 比热容 | The heat needed to raise the temperature of 1 g of a substance by 1°C, q = mcΔT | 使 1 克物质温度升高 1°C 所需的热量。 | Calorimetry uses q = mcΔT with water's specific heat capacity. | 2
- Hess's law | 盖斯定律 | The enthalpy change of a reaction is the sum of enthalpy changes of steps that add to it | 反应焓变等于各步反应焓变之和，与路径无关。 | Hess's law lets us combine known reactions to find ΔH for a new one. | 3

@unit 7 | Equilibrium | 化学平衡
- chemical equilibrium | 化学平衡 | The state in which forward and reverse reaction rates are equal and concentrations remain constant | 正逆反应速率相等、各物质浓度保持不变的状态（动态平衡）。 | At equilibrium, reactions continue in both directions at equal rates. | 2 | #04-014
  mis: At equilibrium, reactions stop — they continue at equal rates.
  mis: At equilibrium, reactant and product concentrations are equal — they are constant, not necessarily equal.
- equilibrium constant | 平衡常数 | The ratio of product to reactant concentrations (activities) at equilibrium, each raised to its coefficient | 平衡时产物浓度幂之积与反应物浓度幂之积的比值，只随温度变化。 | A large K means products are favored at equilibrium. | 3 | #04-015
  vs: reaction quotient
- reaction quotient | 反应商 | The same ratio as K but calculated at any moment, used to predict the direction of shift | 任意时刻按 K 的表达式计算的比值；Q < K 时正向进行，Q > K 时逆向进行。 | Because Q < K, the reaction proceeds forward. | 3
  vs: equilibrium constant
- Le Châtelier's principle | 勒夏特列原理 | A system at equilibrium shifts to partially counteract a disturbance | 平衡体系受到干扰时，会向减弱该干扰的方向移动。 | Adding reactant shifts the equilibrium toward products. | 2 | #04-016
- solubility product | 溶度积 | The equilibrium constant for dissolving a sparingly soluble ionic compound, Ksp | 难溶离子化合物溶解平衡的平衡常数。 | A smaller Ksp indicates lower solubility for salts with the same ion ratio. | 3

@unit 8 | Acids and Bases | 酸与碱
- pH | pH 值 | The negative base-10 logarithm of hydrogen ion concentration | 氢离子浓度的负对数，pH 每降低 1，[H⁺] 增大 10 倍。 | A solution with pH 3 has ten times the [H⁺] of a solution with pH 4. | 1
- strong acid | 强酸 | An acid that ionizes completely in water | 在水中完全电离的酸，如 HCl、HNO₃。 | HCl is a strong acid, so [H⁺] equals its initial concentration. | 2
  vs: weak acid
- weak acid | 弱酸 | An acid that ionizes only partially in water | 在水中部分电离的酸，存在电离平衡，用 Ka 表示。 | Acetic acid is a weak acid with Ka about 1.8 × 10⁻⁵. | 2
  vs: strong acid
- conjugate base | 共轭碱 | The species formed when an acid donates a proton | 酸失去一个质子后形成的物质。 | Acetate is the conjugate base of acetic acid. | 2
- buffer | 缓冲溶液 | A solution of a weak acid and its conjugate base that resists changes in pH | 由弱酸及其共轭碱组成、能抵抗 pH 变化的溶液。 | Blood is a buffer that keeps pH near 7.4. | 3 | #04-017
- equivalence point | 等当点 | The point in a titration where moles of titrant exactly react with moles of analyte | 滴定中滴定剂与被测物恰好完全反应的点。 | For a weak acid titrated with a strong base, the pH at the equivalence point is above 7. | 3
  vs: half-equivalence point
- half-equivalence point | 半当量点 | The point where half the acid has been neutralized, so pH = pKa | 一半酸被中和时，pH = pKa。 | The pKa of the acid can be read at the half-equivalence point. | 3
  vs: equivalence point

@unit 9 | Applications of Thermodynamics | 热力学的应用
- entropy | 熵 | A measure related to the dispersal of energy and the number of possible microstates | 与能量分散和微观状态数相关的量；气体比液体熵大。 | Melting ice increases entropy. | 2 | #04-010
- Gibbs free energy | 吉布斯自由能 | ΔG = ΔH − TΔS; a negative value indicates a thermodynamically favorable process | 恒温恒压下判断反应自发性的状态函数，ΔG < 0 为热力学有利。 | A reaction with ΔH > 0 and ΔS > 0 becomes favorable at high temperature. | 3 | #04-011
  mis: Thermodynamically favorable means fast — favorability says nothing about rate.
- galvanic cell | 原电池 | An electrochemical cell that generates electrical energy from a spontaneous redox reaction | 利用自发氧化还原反应产生电能的装置，阳极发生氧化。 | In a galvanic cell, electrons flow from the anode to the cathode. | 3
  vs: electrolytic cell
- electrolytic cell | 电解池 | An electrochemical cell that uses electrical energy to drive a nonspontaneous reaction | 用外加电能驱动非自发反应的装置。 | Electroplating uses an electrolytic cell. | 3
  vs: galvanic cell

@q chem-u3-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | MCQ | 3 | 2 | intermolecular forces
? When water boils, what is overcome?
=* Hydrogen bonds and other intermolecular forces between water molecules :: Correct — boiling separates molecules.
= Covalent O–H bonds within water molecules :: Boiling does not break water molecules apart.
= Ionic bonds between H⁺ and OH⁻ :: Water is molecular, not ionic.
= Nuclear forces :: Nuclear forces are irrelevant to phase changes.
! Phase changes overcome intermolecular forces, not intramolecular (covalent) bonds.
!zh 相变克服的是分子间作用力，而不是分子内的共价键。
@q chem-u7-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | SCENARIO | 7 | 2 | Le Châtelier's principle
? For N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) ⇌ 2NH₃(g), what happens if the volume of the container is decreased at constant temperature?
=* The equilibrium shifts toward NH₃ because there are fewer gas moles on that side. :: Correct — higher pressure favors fewer moles of gas.
= The equilibrium shifts toward N₂ and H₂. :: That side has more gas moles.
= K increases. :: K depends only on temperature.
= Nothing happens. :: Changing volume changes partial pressures, so Q ≠ K.
! Decreasing volume raises pressure; the system shifts toward fewer moles of gas to counteract it.
!zh 减小体积使压强增大，平衡向气体分子数少的方向移动。
@q chem-u9-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | MCQ | 9 | 3 | Gibbs free energy
? A reaction has ΔG° < 0 but occurs extremely slowly at room temperature. What is the best explanation?
= The reaction is not thermodynamically favorable. :: ΔG° < 0 means it is favorable.
=* The reaction has a high activation energy. :: Correct — thermodynamics says nothing about rate.
= The reaction has a positive ΔH. :: ΔH does not determine rate.
= The equilibrium constant is less than 1. :: ΔG° < 0 implies K > 1.
! Thermodynamic favorability (ΔG) and kinetics (rate, Ea) are separate. Diamond → graphite is favorable but extremely slow.
!zh 热力学有利（ΔG）与动力学（速率、活化能）是两回事，例如金刚石转化为石墨有利但极慢。

@pair oxidation-vs-reduction | oxidation | reduction
! Oxidation is LOSS of electrons (oxidation number increases); reduction is GAIN of electrons (oxidation number decreases). OIL RIG.
!zh 氧化：失电子（氧化数升高）；还原：得电子（氧化数降低）。口诀 OIL RIG。
s: A :: Fe → Fe³⁺ + 3e⁻ :: Electrons lost.
s: B :: Cl₂ + 2e⁻ → 2Cl⁻ :: Electrons gained.
s: A :: The anode of a galvanic cell. :: Oxidation occurs at the anode.
s: B :: The oxidation number of Mn drops from +7 to +2. :: Decrease = reduction.
@pair k-vs-q | equilibrium constant | reaction quotient
! K uses equilibrium concentrations and is fixed at a given temperature; Q uses current concentrations and tells you which way the reaction will shift.
!zh K 使用平衡浓度，温度一定时不变；Q 使用当前浓度，用于判断反应方向。
s: B :: Calculated right after extra reactant is added. :: Non-equilibrium moment.
s: A :: Changes only when temperature changes. :: K depends on temperature only.
s: B :: Compared to K to predict the direction of shift. :: That is Q.
s: A :: Ratio measured once the system stops changing. :: Equilibrium values.
